OL,3,GNEWSAWhy is cracking clay causing train
OL,4,Atroubles?
OL,5,
OL,6,FA summer of record-breaking
OL,7,Ftemperatures is drawing to a close -
OL,8,Fwith the prolonged heat and lack of
OL,9,Frainfall having taken its toll on the
OL,10,Fland beneath us.
OL,12,FRail bosses say the clay that sits
OL,13,Funder the railway in Essex has dried
OL,14,Fout and shrunk because of the weather,
OL,15,Fleading to issues with the quality of
OL,16,Fthe track.
OL,18,FEarlier this month, a train derailed in
OL,19,FLewes, Sussex, injuring 30 people,
OL,20,Ffollowed by another derailment in
OL,21,FWickford just over 24 hours later.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
